# Feature landing pages (site architecture — always)

Patron feature landings (VIP reserV, floqCast, ShoutOut, BartR, RydR, Mingl, FloqAi when it is a product page) share **one** header + chrome pattern. Same color scheme, same hierarchy, **different feature icon only**.

Resume: `@feature-landing$` / `$feature-landing$`.

## Canonical header stack (top → bottom)

Match **VIP reserV** (`vip.html`) as the reference:

1. **Back** — `floqrGlobalBack` / `FLOQRNav.applyGlobalBack` (← Back to Search). No hardcoded `?v=` in the href.
2. **FLOQR parent logo** — `images/floqr-color.png` via `.product-parent-logo` inside `.product-brand-stack` (**centered, alone on its row**).
3. **Feature icon** — stacked **under** FLOQR (not beside it). Use a black-face hero tile when the Search mark is mark-only:
   - VIP → chrome pack via `data-floqr-chrome-icon="vipReserv"` (`images/chrome/vip-nightlife.jpg` / `vip-traditional.jpg`)
   - floqCast → `images/floqcast-hero-icon.svg` (mark: `floqcast-icon.svg`)
   - Classes: `product-logo {feature}-hero-logo` (~160×120 max, pink/cyan drop-shadow). Load `floqr-chrome-scheme.js` on landings that use `data-floqr-chrome-icon`.
4. **Feature title + `?`** — one flex row (`.{feature}-title-row`): `<h1>` + `details.help-popout` summary `?`. Intro / how-to copy lives **inside** the `?`, not as a long paragraph under the title (VIP pattern).
5. **Body card** — glass card from `styles.css` / product chrome. Section heads that need help use the same `?` row pattern (`.{feature}-section-head`).

### Forbidden header layouts

- Feature icon **on the same line** as the FLOQR logo (old floqCast `floqcast-brand-row` / FloqAi-inline pattern on product landings).
- Legacy `suprstr-logo.png` / SupRstR art as the floqCast mark — use `floqcast-icon.svg` / `floqcast-hero-icon.svg` everywhere.
- Flat admin `#111` body on product landings — see `design-notes-product-chrome.mdc`.

## Color / chrome

Same tokens as Search / ShoutOut (`--hot` `#f43abf`, `--accent` `#26d8ff`, pink+cyan radial washes). Primary CTA = hot→accent gradient. Do not invent a second theme per feature.

## Venue / contextual search

When the landing needs venue pick:

- Prefer the **VIP-style** contextual search: search input + result cards (“Select venue”), not a bare orphan `<select>` as the only UI.
- Copy: only clubs with that feature enabled appear (parity with ShoutOut / VIP / floqCast gates).
- Hidden `<select>` may remain as a sync target for existing JS if needed.

## Icons — one mark, two surfaces

| Surface | Asset shape |
|---|---|
| Search tile face | Chrome pack JPG/PNG via `data-floqr-chrome-icon` (HTML face supplies black when needed) |
| Feature landing hero | Same chrome pack as Search for VIP; other features use hero SVG/JPG sized as VIP hero |
| Display / idle (floqCast board) | Newest FloqCAST chrome nightlife JPG (`display-app.js` `FLOQCAST_LOGO` → `images/chrome/floqcast-nightlife.jpg`) |

Replace retired logos site-wide when a mark ships — do not leave `suprstr-logo.png` on landings.

## Checklist (new or edited feature landing)

- [ ] Header order: Back → FLOQR → feature icon (below) → title + `?`
- [ ] Feature icon is the current mark (not a side-by-side FloqAi row)
- [ ] `?` uses `details.help-popout` / FloqAi help repository id
- [ ] Body wash = product chrome; card = glass
- [ ] Venue pick uses search+cards when venue list exists
- [ ] No hardcoded `?v=` in nav links; asset tags re-stamped by bump script
- [ ] Update `docs/FEATURE-WIRING.md` if the landing contract changed

